{{also|left-over|left over}}
==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|left over}}, {{l|en|left-over}}

===Etymology===
From {{m|en|left||remaining", "abandoned}} + {{m|en|over||excess}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# [[remaining|Remaining]]; left behind; [[extra]]; in [[reserve]].
#: ''Do you want some of the '''leftover''' supplies from the event?''
# {{lb|en|chiefly|in the plural|usually|of food}} Remaining after a meal is complete or eaten for a later meal or snack.
#: ''I have some '''leftover''' spaghetti in the fridge, so I don't plan to cook tonight.''
#: ''Not '''leftovers''' again.''

====Usage notes====
* When used after a verb (as part of a predicate phrase), use two separate words:
*: ''I can walk for miles and still have energy [[left over]].''

